  "answer_text": "Here is how you can log in to your **My Service Canada Account (MSCA)**:\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd17 Direct Login Link\n\ud83d\udc49 **[Click here to sign in to My Service Canada Account (MSCA)](https://www.canada.ca/en/employment-social-development/services/my-account.html)**\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd11 Ways to Sign In\n\nThere are several ways you can log in to your MSCA:\n\n1. **GCKey**\nGCKey allows you to access multiple Government of Canada online services. You can use your GCKey username and password to sign in.\n\n2. **Interac\u00ae Sign-In Partner (Banking Login)**\nInterac\u00ae Sign-In Partner allows you to register or sign in using your online banking sign-in information to access MSCA.\n\n3. **Provincial Sign-In**\nYou can access My Service Canada Account (MSCA) by signing in or registering with your provincial sign-in. Note: This service is only available for residents of Alberta and British Columbia.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udccb New User? How to Register\n\nIf you don't have an account yet, you'll need:\n- A Social Insurance Number (SIN) to create an account.\n- You can create a GCKey username and password if you don't already have one by clicking \"Start your registration.\"\n- A **Personal Access Code (PAC)**: PACs are used to verify your identity when registering for MSCA. If you already applied for CPP/OAS benefits, your PAC has been sent to you by mail.\n\n---\n\n### \u26a0\ufe0f Important Reminder\nYou must access and use MSCA only as yourself. No one is authorized to use or create an account on your behalf.\n\nIf you have trouble signing in, visit the [Canada.ca Help Page](https://www.canada.ca/en/employment-social-development/services/my-account.html) for support.",
